## Instructions
- Work through this whole grouped issue in one invocation. Read AGENTS.md,
  PRD.md and relevant code; use `bd show {{taskId}} --json` for evidence notes
  when needed. Preserve unrelated work and stay on the current branch.
- Size work for a context window of up to 200k: aim for about 150k working
  context, reserving the rest for startup, tools, verification and repair. These are
  planning targets, not enforced limits. Read source/evidence on demand.
- Implementation, debugging, required checks and local Beads updates are already
  authorized. Older planning-only notes do not require renewed approval.
- Finish autonomously. Do not ask for implementation permission or make routine
  design choices into user-approval gates. Choose the simplest reasonable default
  consistent with PRD.md and record the decision and tradeoff in the issue notes.
  Older issue/proposal wording asking for agreement on routine choices is
  superseded by this authorization; it is not a reason to stop or mark blocked.
  Honor current explicit user constraints, release order and acceptance checks.
  Owner authorization does not grant third-party approval or authorize unrelated
  destructive actions, credential relocation or bypassing runtime restrictions.
- Implement the acceptance criteria and run the checks relevant to this issue.
  If already implemented, verify the existing behavior. Fix recoverable failures
  within this task; record actual evidence and distinguish fixtures from live checks.
- Prefer integration checks. Use browser/E2E checks where acceptance requires
  them. Run `npm test` plus only the verify scripts named in the acceptance
  criteria or covering the files you changed; do not run the full
  `npm run verify` unless the acceptance criteria ask for it. Run
  `npm run test:render` only when the change touches video rendering. Restore
  regenerated `docs/verification/` files the task does not need as evidence. Keep internal steps and acceptance review in this same issue. Split only
  for a separate deliverable, external/user gate or demonstrated context limit;
  record a precise checkpoint before a retry instead of creating microtasks.
{{#if config.autoCommit}}
- Ralph creates the Git commit after completion, outside the agent sandbox.
  Do not stage or commit from the agent. Read-only `.git` is expected.
{{else}}
- Review and commit only this task's changes locally; preserve unrelated edits.
{{/if}}

## Completion
After the acceptance checks pass, record the result in the issue notes and
append it to the end of `.ralph-tui/progress.md`, then run:
```
bd close {{taskId}} --reason "Verified result"
bd export -o .beads/issues.jsonl
```
The export lets BV link the closed issue to the implementation commit.
Only after these steps succeed, end the response with:
<promise>COMPLETE</promise>
{{#if config.autoCommit}}
The commit is pending until Ralph performs it after your response.
{{/if}}

If unfinished, record the exact remaining work in the issue notes and end without
the completion signal; Ralph reopens and retries the issue.
Before declaring a blocker, diagnose the cause and try reasonable permitted
recovery paths: inspect relevant code/configuration, repair task-owned defects,
check runtime/storage access, and use another already-authorized provider for
shared checks when available. A failed first attempt, routine uncertainty,
missing implementation, or a request for renewed permission is not a blocker.
Continue all independent work within this issue. Do not wait indefinitely or
repeat quota/auth failures without new evidence, and never substitute fixtures
for required native evidence or weaken acceptance to claim completion.
Mark blocked only when a concrete external prerequisite still prevents required
work after these attempts. Record the exact failure, attempted remedies and
results, remaining acceptance, and actionable resolution/retry condition. Link
an existing resolution issue or create one if none exists. Keep umbrella epics
open while children carry blockers; a blocked parent can hide its own recovery
tasks from the ready queue. Preserve real technical dependency edges.
Do not emit the completion signal for unfinished work. Ralph selects the next
issue; do not start another task. Keep all operations local; no push or bd sync.

Shared checks may use either working provider. Provider-specific acceptance and
the full text release require the explicit Claude/Codex evidence in the issue.
